WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.763
Meet BrostCo.

00:00:01.763 --> 00:00:05.779
Follow a government contracting workflow, from
opportunity to review.

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:10.346
Start with opportunities that fit your business.

00:00:10.346 --> 00:00:15.124
Here, we switch to a focused list, then open the
same sample pursuit.

00:00:15.124 --> 00:00:21.269
Fit, deadline, and the source context stay
connected, so you can inspect the details behind
the match.

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:29.520
A match is only a starting point.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:36.910
Open the requirements, check what needs
attention, and return to the opportunity
overview without losing context.

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:41.807
This sample record contains staged analysis, not
a live AI result.

00:00:41.807 --> 00:00:45.135
Your team checks the underlying documents before
committing.

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:50.231
Keep the subcontractor and the work together.

00:00:50.231 --> 00:00:55.408
Move from the company record to related
opportunities, then inspect its recorded quotes.

00:00:55.408 --> 00:00:59.026
Contacts, conversations, and pricing remain
connected.

00:00:59.026 --> 00:01:02.997
Subcontractor outreach is optional and follows
your company's rules.

00:01:02.997 --> 00:01:05.553
No outreach is sent in this demonstration.

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:10.472
Read the latest reply with its conversation
nearby.

00:01:10.472 --> 00:01:15.996
Expand earlier messages when you need the
background, then collapse them to focus again.

00:01:15.996 --> 00:01:18.876
These messages are sample history.

00:01:18.876 --> 00:01:23.698
Reading a thread does not send a reply, and a
draft is not a delivered message.

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:32.325
Open the subcontractor coverage, inspect the
sample quote, then move into pricing.

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:37.521
Keep amounts, assumptions, requirements, and
missing inputs with the pursuit.

00:01:37.521 --> 00:01:40.358
This is a review workflow, not a submitted bid.

00:01:40.358 --> 00:01:44.848
Your team confirms pricing, reviews terms,
signs, and submits.

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:51.488
Open a recorded event to see the details behind
the activity.

00:01:51.488 --> 00:01:55.058
Use filters when you need to narrow the history.

00:01:55.058 --> 00:01:59.316
The ledger distinguishes recorded outcomes from
work still waiting.

00:01:59.316 --> 00:02:06.154
Sample records illustrate the interface here; no
external messages, payments, or bids were sent.

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:09.729
Your rules guide automation.

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:11.842
Your team keeps final review.

00:02:11.842 --> 00:02:14.216
Start your free trial at BrostCo.
